From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:05:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: cdc_ncm: enable 64KB SuperSpeed NTB aggregation and lower aggregation delay for 5G mobile tethering

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

Default Linux cdc_ncm clamps NTB buffer sizes to 16KB (CDC_NCM_NTB_DEF_SIZE_RX/TX),
artificially restricting transfer aggregation on SuperSpeed USB 3.0 links.
Modern 5G SA modems exchange 32KB-64KB NTBs; 16KB clamping forces excessive URB
interrupts and limits downlink throughput.

This MAXNET patch:
1. Dynamically scales def_rx and def_tx up to 64KB for USB_SPEED_SUPER devices.
2. Lowers aggregation timer from 400us to 125us for reduced interactive latency.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ncm.c
@@ -706,10 +706,22 @@
 	/* be conservative when selecting initial buffer size to
 	 * increase the number of hosts this will work for
 	 */
-	def_rx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_DEF_SIZE_RX,
-		       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbInMaxSize));
-	def_tx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_DEF_SIZE_TX,
-		       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbOutMaxSize));
+	/* MAXNET SuperSpeed Mobile Tethering Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+	 * Scale initial NTB buffer sizes up to 64KB for SuperSpeed USB 3.0+ 5G modems
+	 * and smartphones to achieve multi-gigabit throughput with low CPU overhead.
+	 * Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
+	 */
+	if (dev->udev->speed >= USB_SPEED_SUPER) {
+		def_rx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_MAX_SIZE_RX,
+			       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbInMaxSize));
+		def_tx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_MAX_SIZE_TX,
+			       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbOutMaxSize));
+	} else {
+		def_rx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_DEF_SIZE_RX,
+			       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbInMaxSize));
+		def_tx = min_t(u32, CDC_NCM_NTB_DEF_SIZE_TX,
+			       le32_to_cpu(ctx->ncm_parm.dwNtbOutMaxSize));
+	}
 
 	/* clamp rx_max and tx_max and inform device */
 	cdc_ncm_update_rxtx_max(dev, def_rx, def_tx);
--- a/include/linux/usb/cdc_ncm.h
+++ b/include/linux/usb/cdc_ncm.h
@@ -80,7 +80,8 @@
 /* Restart the timer, if amount of datagrams is less than given value */
 #define	CDC_NCM_RESTART_TIMER_DATAGRAM_CNT	3
 #define	CDC_NCM_TIMER_PENDING_CNT		2
-#define CDC_NCM_TIMER_INTERVAL_USEC		400UL
+/* MAXNET: 125us aggregation interval for responsive 5G SuperSpeed mobile tethering */
+#define CDC_NCM_TIMER_INTERVAL_USEC		125UL
 #define CDC_NCM_TIMER_INTERVAL_MIN		5UL
 #define CDC_NCM_TIMER_INTERVAL_MAX		(U32_MAX / NSEC_PER_USEC)
 
